>>I've recently started playing NetHack and can't decide which character
>>class(es) are most likely to do well - my favourites thus far are Samurai
>>or Wizards. Has anyone out there got any suggestions/advice?
>>Replies via Notes or e-mail welcome!

I used to prefer to start with a Barbarian, but recently I've decided that
Wizard is the best class for a beginner.

SPOILERS FOLLOW...


Since the wizard starts with an Athame (sp?), and athames _NEVER_ get dull,
a wizard can engrave Elbereth any time (except when blinded) with total
success. For example, before quaffing at a fountain, I always engrave
Elbereth in the ground first. That way, if the snakes or a water demon
emerge, I am protected. Likewise, I always engrave Elbereth before eating
a monster or reading a book or scroll. In the beginning levels, there are
no breath weapons to worry about, so barring the occasional thrown dagger,
Elbereth is excellent protection.

Wizards can acquire decent armour fairly early on by killing a dwarf
fighter. I like to start with a ring of regeneration, since you can
engrave Elbereth in the middle of a fight, wait until your hit points
are at max, and then start fighting again.


